# Playa AI — environment variable reference
# Copy relevant variables to .env.local for local development.
# Never commit real secrets or API keys to this file.

# ── Get Involved form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider-neutral form submission endpoint for the /get-involved page.
# The form posts FormData with Accept: application/json using fetch().
# Compatible with providers that accept multipart form data and return JSON
# (e.g. Formspree, Getform, Basin, Netlify Forms, a custom server route).
#
# If absent or blank:
#   - No network request is made.
#   - The form shows an "Online submission temporarily unavailable" state.
#   - A mailto:hello@playa-ai.org fallback is displayed with the selected path
#     pre-populated in the email subject line.
#
# To configure:
#   1. Choose an approved provider (do not use providers that require a secret
#      key inside frontend JavaScript — VITE_ variables are public).
#   2. Set the endpoint URL here.
#   3. Test with synthetic data and confirm receipt at hello@playa-ai.org.
#   4. Redeploy.
#
# Audit item #28 status:
#   - Page, form, and 7 participation sections: IMPLEMENTED
#   - Email delivery: PENDING (requires this variable to be configured)
#   - Confirmed receipt: PENDING (requires a real production delivery test)
VITE_GET_INVOLVED_FORM_ENDPOINT=
